{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437403-eating-my-agg-flakes-for-a-complete-breakfast","id":437403,"title":"Eating My Agg Flakes for a Complete Breakfast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-11T12:57:21-07:00","id":437403,"title":"Eating My Agg Flakes for a Complete Breakfast","content":"I was going through the werewolf 2.0 and came across an odd revelation. <br /> <br /> So Savage Rending and Silver Jaws are out. <br /> <br /> I was wondering, since Gauru werewolves cannot be stopped without Aggravated Damage, how do you deal aggravated? Do you carry silver? That can be difficult, as you have to either craft it, or find someone who can and be able to afford it, then carry it around without your buddies getting mad. <br /> <br /> So I saw in the section about getting essence, that when you eat someone for essence, you deal aggravated. <br /> <br /> I just wanted to see if this was the case. The primary method of dealing aggravated damage is to eat someone, whereby the normally lethal damage bite becomes aggravated as you gulp down hunks of their meaty goodness? <br /> <br /> This isn't specified as being particular to human or wolf, but makes me wonder two things. <br /> <br /> 1. Is the decision to swallow whats in your mouth when you are ripping a werewolf apart mystically enhance the wound?<br /> <br /> 2. If so, it means that any werewolf willing to take the Harmony breaking point is chomping for aggravated, which could be very interesting in the Pure vs Forsaken landscape. <br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:07:45-07:00","id":437427,"title":"","content":"I don't have the book with me so forgive me if I'm wrong, but isn't the eating-for-essence only when on Siskur-dah? There is a certain absolute and primordial callback going on there which I would argue might make the miniscule difference? Also, practically, you a) aren't likely to stop eating halfway through and let your prey leave and b) if it wasn't agg you couldn't eat some things fast enough to stop them from regenning back too fast for it to be effective, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:16:13-07:00","id":437434,"title":"","content":"The primary method of dealing aggravated damage to a werewolf in Gauru form is hitting them very hard or many times with numerous assailants. Silver is the secondary method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-11-2015, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:45:59-07:00","id":437481,"title":"","content":"Consuming flesh for essence is a constant with cannibalism. I don't believe you need siskur dah, but you definitely violate the path doing it. You're willing and knowingly eatin someone. Not just bite and spit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:52:09-07:00","id":437485,"title":"","content":"This is explicitly suggested as a thing you can do on page 285.<br /> <br /> It actually works quite well, because silver breaks you towards flesh, but cannibalism breaks you towards spirit. Get the right rhythm going and you can keep your harmony pretty good whist murdering werewolves with impunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-11-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:02:37-07:00","id":437507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437403-eating-my-agg-flakes-for-a-complete-breakfast?p=437485#post437485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is explicitly suggested as a thing you can do on page 285.<br /> <br /> It actually works quite well, because silver breaks you towards flesh, but cannibalism breaks you towards spirit. Get the right rhythm going and you can keep your harmony pretty good whist murdering werewolves with impunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your only consequences at that point are social ones, which are an entirely different and dangerous matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:06:26-07:00","id":437510,"title":"","content":"On page 100 it says that when you eat humans and wolves for essence, it deals aggravated damage. <br /> <br /> Like Elfive mentioned, 285 answers my question. It says under the Cannibalism section that eating a werewolf deals aggravated. <br /> <br /> Thanks Elfive, that's what I was looking for, I appreciate the fine research skillz. <br /> <br /> But yeah, its the 'eat the baby now' issue, where you can float with those. however, there is a 'soft control' written in under the Oath of the Moon section, which talks about how breaking the Oath of the Moon basically ostracizes you from society, makes spirits hate you and makes life miserable altogether. So, you could technically eat people, then use silver, then eat people and not have to worry about being out of balance, you won't be in a pack anymore, unless you're all a bunch of crazies, in which case the local Blood Talons will call their own Siskur Dah to hunt the Oathbreakers, and good luck getting any renown, as no Lune is going to get near you without serious contrition. <br /> <br /> Hmm...interesting dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:06:36-07:00","id":437511,"title":"","content":"Keep that up and you'll be featured on Uratha's Most Wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:07:38-07:00","id":437513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437403-eating-my-agg-flakes-for-a-complete-breakfast?p=437485#post437485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It actually works quite well, because silver breaks you towards flesh, but cannibalism breaks you towards spirit. Get the right rhythm going and you can keep your harmony pretty good whist murdering werewolves with impunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as no one realizes what you are doing; it isn't likely to be popular among the People. Obviously it depends on the pack and story but if stories about such a werewolf get out than they might find themselves the target of scared hunts by packs of Blood Talons and any number of Pure packs. No specific penalities in mecahnics but potentally serious narrative drawbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:09:07-07:00","id":437518,"title":"","content":"On the other hand I think we just figured out how the Predator Kings stay balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:18:34-07:00","id":437527,"title":"","content":"If you're fortunate enough to be in Wroclaw, Poland you can go join the Lodge of the Field and feast upon flesh until your heart's content! You'll be part of a dominant faction whose entire ideology promotes cannibalism as a holy ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:33:08-07:00","id":437539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437403-eating-my-agg-flakes-for-a-complete-breakfast?p=437518#post437518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand I think we just figured out how the Predator Kings stay balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Have you hear the story of Ulfric Blood-Drink? They say the bastard goes into battle with a silver knife and fork set.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:45:11-07:00","id":437554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437403-eating-my-agg-flakes-for-a-complete-breakfast#post437403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going through the werewolf 2.0 and came across an odd revelation.<br /> <br /> So Savage Rending and Silver Jaws are out.<br /> <br /> I was wondering, since Gauru werewolves cannot be stopped without Aggravated Damage, how do you deal aggravated? Do you carry silver? That can be difficult, as you have to either craft it, or find someone who can and be able to afford it, then carry it around without your buddies getting mad.<br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weapons of any kind, and lots of friends to use them. If you want to go Gauru hunting you only need on average three mortals with semi-automatic weapons for every pack member. As long as they focus one wolf after the next and keep the hell away from melee, they will be very efficient Gauru killing machines. You don't even need Willpower use, though it helps.<br /> <br /> In a melee fight where you don't care if they die because they are hell bent on fighting to their last man because self preservation is for the week, add an extra mortal for similar results.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It appears to be hard to mangle a Gauru. It is not in statistical actuality. You just need bigger numbers or multiple actions. However, don't put Gauru on a pedestal. It's meant to be badass and an ace in the hole for Werewolves. One on one fights between Werewolves should be close, brutal and rare. Werewolves usually have a pack. Never leave home without one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:13:05-07:00","id":437604,"title":"","content":"Ah, the Imperial Guardsman method. That'd do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:17:49-07:00","id":437610,"title":"","content":"&quot;But our flashlights, I mean lasguns, only tell them where we are sir. They, like these goggles, do nothing.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the 3 vs 1 is off by a bit. remember Gauru gets defense vs firearms, with an average defense of 6. Also, going to need a bigger gun than a sub-machine gun. But yeah, dog pile, or something huge and scary that only takes bashing from normal werewolf attacks like a lot of bigger spirits, that also have minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:43:37-07:00","id":437654,"title":"","content":"There's a Rite, URFARAH\u2019S BANE (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:33:53-07:00","id":437697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437403-eating-my-agg-flakes-for-a-complete-breakfast?p=437610#post437610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;But our flashlights, I mean lasguns, only tell them where we are sir. They, like these goggles, do nothing.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the 3 vs 1 is off by a bit. remember Gauru gets defense vs firearms, with an average defense of 6. Also, going to need a bigger gun than a sub-machine gun. But yeah, dog pile, or something huge and scary that only takes bashing from normal werewolf attacks like a lot of bigger spirits, that also have minions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Defense averages around four for most average Werewolves, even in Gauru, and I did factor into the Defense versus Firearms. Medium and Long Bursts really seal the deal for them dice pools, even with the penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:06:57-07:00","id":437727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437403-eating-my-agg-flakes-for-a-complete-breakfast?p=437554#post437554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weapons of any kind, and lots of friends to use them. If you want to go Gauru hunting you only need on average three mortals with semi-automatic weapons for every pack member. As long as they focus one wolf after the next and keep the hell away from melee, they will be very efficient Gauru killing machines. You don't even need Willpower use, though it helps.<br /> <br /> In a melee fight where you don't care if they die because they are hell bent on fighting to their last man because self preservation is for the week, add an extra mortal for similar results.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It appears to be hard to mangle a Gauru. It is not in statistical actuality. You just need bigger numbers or multiple actions. However, don't put Gauru on a pedestal. It's meant to be badass and an ace in the hole for Werewolves. One on one fights between Werewolves should be close, brutal and rare. Werewolves usually have a pack. Never leave home without one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they are close to being his equals, a werewolf in Gauru can use D&amp;D(ooooops!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smili